= Found the Office of Sectarian Affairs

We attempted to establish the Office of Sectarian Affairs during the first İnönü government after 27 May, but failed to do so under those coalition governments. The office is intended to provide services to Muslims of different sects. Most importantly, it will recognize Alevism as a sect rather than merely a local folk culture, and officially recognize cemevis, the places of worship and assembly used by Alevi communities, as places of worship. This would be a major step toward ending the social and state repression that Alevi communities have suffered since the Ottoman era, bringing us closer to Kemalism's half-century-old goal of ending that repression.

- @root: Continue.

